<div class="docs-architecture-page">

    <div class="docs-eyebrow">
        ENGINE / PROJECT STRUCTURE
    </div>

    <h1>
        Project <span class="docs-accent">architecture</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        Crafty is a layered application, not a general-purpose engine
        with a game built on top. The runtime is intentionally shaped
        around the needs of this voxel game.
    </p>

    <h2>Project dependency map</h2>

    <div class="docs-architecture">
        <div class="docs-arch-node docs-arch-game">
            <span class="docs-arch-label">APPLICATION</span>
            <b>Crafty</b>
            <small>Game executable · gameplay, content, player, assets</small>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-arch-arrow">
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-down"></i>
            <small>references</small>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-arch-grid">
            <div class="docs-arch-node">
                <span class="docs-arch-label">RUNTIME</span>
                <b>CraftyNative</b>
                <small>Runtime, ECS, rendering, UI</small>
            </div>

            <div class="docs-arch-node">
                <span class="docs-arch-label">PUBLIC API</span>
                <b>Crafty.SDK</b>
                <small>Public mod contracts</small>
            </div>

            <div class="docs-arch-node">
                <span class="docs-arch-label">WORLD SYSTEMS</span>
                <b>Crafty.ChunkGeneration</b>
                <small>World and chunk generation</small>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-arch-arrow">
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-down"></i>
            <small>graphics dependency</small>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-arch-node docs-arch-sdk">
            <span class="docs-arch-label">GRAPHICS FOUNDATION</span>
            <b>Vulcan</b>
            <small>
                Low-level graphics device, buffers, shaders, and pipelines
                · external source tree
            </small>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-architecture-note">
        <i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i>
        <div>
            <strong>Dependency direction matters</strong>
            <p>
                <code>Crafty.SDK</code> has no project references.
                <code>Crafty.ChunkGeneration</code> references the SDK;
                <code>CraftyNative</code> references the chunk-generation
                project and Vulcan; and the game references the runtime,
                SDK, and chunk-generation library.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What each layer owns</h2>

    <p>
        Each project has a distinct responsibility. Understanding these
        boundaries is important when navigating the source or deciding
        which APIs should be used by external extensions.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-layer-list">

        <article class="docs-layer-card">
            <div class="docs-layer-icon">
                <i class="bi bi-controller"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-layer-body">
                <div class="docs-layer-meta">GAME APPLICATION</div>
                <h3>Crafty <span>— game-specific behavior</span></h3>
                <p>
                    The game project contains components such as
                    <code>Player</code>, <code>Movement</code>,
                    <code>Inventory</code>, <code>Hotbar</code>, and
                    combat-related data.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Its systems implement player movement, collision,
                    block interaction, inventory synchronization, time
                    of day, chunk streaming, lighting updates, and mesh
                    rebuild scheduling. The built-in content mod is
                    under <code>Crafty/MainMod</code>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="docs-layer-card">
            <div class="docs-layer-icon">
                <i class="bi bi-cpu"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-layer-body">
                <div class="docs-layer-meta">ENGINE RUNTIME</div>
                <h3>CraftyNative <span>— runtime services</span></h3>
                <p>
                    The runtime provides <code>Scene</code>, component
                    stores, system interfaces, hierarchy handling,
                    window/input integration, and a job system.
                </p>
                <p>
                    It also contains 3D mesh and world-rendering helpers,
                    the retained-mode UI tree, HUD renderers, sky
                    rendering, and animation helpers.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="docs-layer-card">
            <div class="docs-layer-icon">
                <i class="bi bi-puzzle"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-layer-body">
                <div class="docs-layer-meta">PUBLIC EXTENSION API</div>
                <h3>Crafty.SDK <span>— extension contracts</span></h3>
                <p>
                    The SDK defines the mod entry-point contract and
                    context, content registries, block models,
                    properties and behaviors, items, and
                    world-generation interfaces.
                </p>
                <p>
                    It is separate from the private game and runtime
                    implementation.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="docs-layer-card">
            <div class="docs-layer-icon">
                <i class="bi bi-globe2"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-layer-body">
                <div class="docs-layer-meta">WORLD IMPLEMENTATION</div>
                <h3>Crafty.ChunkGeneration <span>— world implementation</span></h3>
                <p>
                    This project implements <code>World</code>,
                    <code>Chunk</code>, world-generation services,
                    chunk loading, and persistence.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The concrete <code>Chunk</code> type is in this
                    library; the SDK exposes the <code>IChunk</code>
                    contract.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="docs-layer-card">
            <div class="docs-layer-icon">
                <i class="bi bi-gpu-card"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-layer-body">
                <div class="docs-layer-meta">GRAPHICS BACKEND</div>
                <h3>Vulcan <span>— graphics foundation</span></h3>
                <p>
                    The renderer uses Vulcan abstractions and the
                    DirectX backend. The checked-in runtime code
                    creates a graphics device through
                    <code>Vulcan.Vulcan.CreateDevice</code> and uses
                    D3D11-specific command-buffer and swapchain types.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Vulcan is not included in this repository checkout
                    and the solution references an external local path.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

    </div>

    <h2>Technology and build characteristics</h2>

    <p>
        The projects share a modern .NET toolchain, but their build
        settings and native integration requirements differ.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-tech-grid">

        <div class="docs-tech-item">
            <i class="bi bi-code-slash"></i>
            <div>
                <strong>.NET 10</strong>
                <p>
                    C# projects with nullable reference types and
                    implicit usings.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-tech-item">
            <i class="bi bi-lightning-charge"></i>
            <div>
                <strong>Native AOT</strong>
                <p>
                    <code>Crafty</code> enables Native AOT publishing,
                    AOT compatibility analysis, trimming analysis,
                    and unsafe code.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-tech-item">
            <i class="bi bi-memory"></i>
            <div>
                <strong>Low-level runtime</strong>
                <p>
                    <code>CraftyNative</code> allows unsafe code and
                    uses StbImageSharp and StbTrueTypeSharp for
                    image and font loading.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-tech-item">
            <i class="bi bi-window-desktop"></i>
            <div>
                <strong>Windowing and input</strong>
                <p>
                    The game uses Silk.NET input/windowing with
                    GLFW and SDL packages.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-architecture-note">
        <i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i>
        <div>
            <strong>Do not confuse project boundaries with mod boundaries</strong>
            <p>
                A project reference in the solution does not automatically
                mean its types are public mod APIs. For mods, depend on
                documented SDK contracts rather than private
                <code>Crafty</code> or <code>CraftyNative</code> classes.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

